\
In my metadata spreadsheet, I chose to record page orientation and content type for each scanned page of the diary.  \
I made this decision because these two fields highlight both the material and narrative variation within the text.  \
The orientation (horizontal, vertical, or mixed) captures how Hadden used the physical space of the page, which helps reveal shifts between formal diary entries, sketches, and scattered notes.  \
The content type distinguishes whether each page contains continuous writing, drawings, or blank space, allowing patterns in the diary\'92s structure and composition to emerge across the digital facsimile.  \
\
I focused on these categories rather than broader bibliographic data because they offer insights that would be most useful for digital editions and research datasets: they connect the visual layout of each image to the literary and personal content of the diary.  \
Given the diversity of the pages, from prose to landscape sketches to vocabulary lists, these metadata choices help future users navigate the document not only by page number but by type of visual and textual experience.\
